;; og:preserve-this the global instance, scene chain (issue 522): decodes
;; clean at the retail position (this file's own top-level, immediately
;; after the constructor above, matching jak3's twin exactly), landed now
;; that method 12 is too. The raw decode wraps it in a kmemopen/kmemclose
;; pair alongside a separate, unrelated zero-guard init for
;; external-art-control's own global instance; neither the wrapper nor
;; that unrelated init is part of this lane's own chain, so only the one
;; define lands here, matching the brief's own scope.
;;
;; Reachability audit (AGENTS.md rule 5: landing a definition activates its
;; guarded callers), scoped to the boot path and scene-player-init per this
;; lane's own brief, since those are what the scene probe exercises:
;;
;; - Boot path: game-info.gc's own initialize! calls (kill-current-talker
;;   '() '() 'die) unconditionally on every boot (ambient.gc's own
;;   og:preserve-this note on kill-current-talker names this exact call as
;;   the R10 boot crash this instance's own absence used to guard against).
;;   kill-current-talker's body is gated on (nonzero? *gui-control*), the
;;   only such guard on the symbol itself anywhere in goal_src/jakx (grepped
;;   whole-tree); once nonzero, its five calls all reach gui-control-method-
;;   16 (landed) with arg0 hard-coded to the integer 4 in every one of them.
;;   Method 16's own body dispatches gui-control-method-19 (held) via
;;   method-of-object, but only inside an (and (= sv-16 'play) ...) guard,
;;   sv-16 being arg0 itself; comparing an int against the quoted symbol
;;   'play is never true, so this dispatch is unreached from every one of
;;   kill-current-talker's five calls. The same check holds for every other
;;   landed gui-control-method-16 call site in the tree (scene.gc's states,
;;   ambient.gc's talker states, speech.gc): all pass an int literal (2 or
;;   4), never 'play, so the method-19 dispatch is provably unreached from
;;   any currently-landed caller, not just the boot path.
;; - scene-player-init (scene.gc): calls only gui-control-method-9 (landed),
;;   which touches no held method internally (add-connection is an engine
;;   method, unrelated to this audit).
;;
;; Outside this audit's own scope but worth recording: gui-control-method-17
;; (landed) also dispatches gui-control-method-19 internally, and those
;; dispatches are real, condition-gated reachable code, not provably dead
;; like method 16's; method 17 itself is not called from the boot path or
;; scene-player-init (its callers are ambient.gc's talker states and
;; scene.gc's own wait/play-anim states, both post-init). gui-control-
;; method-20 (held) is dispatched from cam-vehicle-crash (a camera-slave
;; state for an actual vehicle crash event) and from a coliseum level
;; object (coliseum-obs-female-statue.gc); neither is boot-path or
;; scene-player-init reachable either. Both are flagged for whoever lands
;; methods 17/19/20 next, not blockers for this instance.
;;
;; og:preserve-this RE-ARMED (issues 522/534): this define was held twice,
;; the second time after an empirical red where the boot crashed at the
;; first gui-control-method-16 dispatch reading a zero slot on a live,
;; validly-typed instance. Root cause was NOT this define or the audit
;; above: the gui-control deftype used to execute in three objects, and
;; the kernel's new_type (kscheme.cpp) zeros every custom slot on every
;; execution, so cam-states.o's copy (DGO 467) wiped the vtable loader.o
;; (248) had filled. The deftype is single-homed in gui-h.gc since issue
;; 540's first slice, and the retirement condition this note's held form
;; carried is fully met: methods 19 and 25 are landed, and the
;; REPL-attached re-probe at that tip read every landed slot nonzero
;; (new at loader-region 0xd26614, methods 9/11/12/14/15/16/17/19/25 all
;; live, unlanded slots exactly 0), constructed a well-formed instance
;; (engine nonzero and typed), and executed the previously-crashing
;; method-16 call to a clean int-0 return with zero crash markers. The
;; boot smoke on this rung is the arming's own empirical gate:
;; kill-current-talker's three method-16 calls run live at every boot
;; from here on.
(define *gui-control* (new 'global 'gui-control 64))

;; og:preserve-this bind *art-control* (issue 522): mirrors jak3 loader.gc:
;; 2726-2728's shape exactly (a zero-guarded set!, not a bare define), the
;; deferred half of this file's own prior note above (the *gui-control*
;; landing explicitly scoped this init out as "a separate, unrelated
;; zero-guard init... not part of this lane's own chain"). The constructor
;; is landed at loader-h.gc:166: it wires the two external-art-buffers to
;; each other (buffer 0's other is buffer 1 and vice versa), clears all
;; three spool-anim rec slots (name #f, priority 1e8, owner handle #f),
;; zeros spool-lock and reserve-buffer/active-stream, and allocates a
;; fresh 4-slot spool-anim boxed-array for queue-stream with length 0.
;; dma-reserve-buffer-count, frame-mask and dma-reserve-heap are left at
;; object-new's zero fill, matching jak3's own constructor.
;;
;; This unblocks three sites that dereference *art-control* unguarded or
;; under a bring-up stopgap: level.gc:2290's own og:preserve-this guard
;; ("*art-control* is defined by the unlanded jakx car-art/loader object;
;; unbound it reads 0") can retire once this define is proven live; play-
;; anim's status dotimes at scene.gc:1626-1631 dereferences (-> *art-
;; control* buffer gp-0 status) with no guard at all; and the wait state's
;; G7 file-status dispatch at scene.gc:1251 calls (file-status *art-
;; control* ...) the same way. All three read goal 0 and fault on a zero
;; *art-control* the moment G3 (the process-grab? wall, issue 522, held
;; separately) clears.
;;
;; external-art-control stays single-homed: its only deftype is loader-
;; h.gc:138, so check_type_singlehome is unaffected by this rung.
(if (zero? *art-control*)
    (set! *art-control* (new 'global 'external-art-control))
    )

;; og:preserve-this add-process: clean decode, no config edits needed on the
;; body itself (the connectable-list-walk-as-connection idiom needed
;; type_casts.jsonc entries to resolve, not a source-level change). Searches
;; the engine's alive-list for a live gui-connection matching channel and
;; name owned by arg0; on a miss, reuses a free-standing slot with a
;; matching channel/name/priority sentinel out of this's own connections
;; array, or mints a new-sound-id, then calls engine's own add-connection.
(defmethod gui-control-method-9 ((this gui-control) (arg0 process) (arg1 int) (arg2 int) (arg3 string) (arg4 float) (arg5 int))
  (let ((sv-32 (the-as connectable #f)))
    (let ((sv-48 (-> this engine alive-list next0)))
      (-> this engine)
      (let ((sv-64 (-> sv-48 next0)))
        (while (!= sv-48 (-> this engine alive-list-end))
          (when (the-as
                  gui-connection
                  (and (= arg1 (the-as gui-connection (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-48) channel)))
                       (string= arg3 (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-48) name))
                       (the-as gui-connection (= ((method-of-type gui-connection get-process) (the-as connection sv-48)) arg0))
                       )
                  )
            (set! sv-32 sv-48)
            (goto cfg-12)
            )
          (set! sv-48 sv-64)
          (-> this engine)
          (set! sv-64 (-> sv-64 next0))
          )
        )
      )
    (label cfg-12)
    (when (not sv-32)
      (let ((sv-16 0))
        (let ((sv-80 32))
          (while (nonzero? sv-80)
            (+! sv-80 -1)
            (let ((sv-20 (-> this connections sv-80)))
              (if (and (nonzero? (-> sv-20 id))
                       (= arg1 (-> sv-20 channel))
                       (string= arg3 (-> sv-20 name))
                       (>= (-> sv-20 priority) -1.0)
                       )
                  (set! sv-16 (the-as int (-> sv-20 id)))
                  )
              )
            )
          )
        (if (zero? sv-16)
            (set! sv-16 (the-as int (new-sound-id)))
            )
        (set! sv-32 (add-connection (-> this engine) arg0 arg4 0 arg3 sv-16))
        )
      (the-as gui-connection (the-as connection sv-32))
      )
    (the-as
      uint
      (cond
        ((the-as gui-connection sv-32)
         (set! (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) priority) arg4)
         (set! (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) channel) (the-as gui-channel arg1))
         (set! (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) action) (the-as gui-action arg2))
         (set! (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) param2) (the-as int arg3))
         (set! (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) hold-time) (the-as time-frame arg5))
         (set! (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) flags) (the-as gui-connection-flags (the-as gui-connection 1)))
         (set! (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) fade) (the-as uint 0))
         (the-as int (-> (the-as gui-connection sv-32) id))
         )
        (else
          (format 0 "ERROR: could not connection ~A to gui engine.~%" arg0)
          0
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )

;; og:preserve-this remove-process (method 10), gui-art pump lane (issue
;; 550/551, secondary per the brief): clean decode once the deftype's own
;; arg count widened () none -> (process gui-channel) int, matching jak3's
;; own twin exactly (this file's own all-types.gc hint comment); no
;; type_casts.jsonc window was needed once the declaration carried the real
;; shape. Walks the alive-list for a live gui-connection whose channel and
;; owning process both match, and moves the first hit to the dead list via
;; the already-landed generic move-to-dead. Has no landed caller in this
;; tree yet (gui-control-method-13, which would dispatch neither this nor
;; the callee below, stays held; see loader.gc's own og:preserve-this note
;; on that method).
(defmethod gui-control-method-10 ((this gui-control) (arg0 process) (arg1 gui-channel))
  (let ((s3-0 (-> this engine alive-list next0)))
    (-> this engine)
    (let ((s2-0 (-> s3-0 next0)))
      (while (!= s3-0 (-> this engine alive-list-end))
        (if (and (= arg1 (-> (the-as gui-connection s3-0) channel))
                 (= arg0 ((method-of-type gui-connection get-process) (the-as connection s3-0)))
                 )
            ((method-of-type gui-connection move-to-dead) (the-as connection s3-0))
            )
        (set! s3-0 s2-0)
